{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Density and Mass Concentration Units.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Density and Mass Concentration Units.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"density and mass concentration units density and mass concentration units","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Density and Mass Concentration Units.md","fileName":"Density and Mass Concentration Units.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Density and Mass Concentration Units","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions","Volume Unit Scaling","Conversion-Factor Chains","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Density and Mass Concentration Units.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Density and Mass Concentration Units.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"density and mass concentration units density and mass concentration units","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Density and Mass Concentration Units.md","fileName":"Density and Mass Concentration Units.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Density and Mass Concentration Units","heading":"Density and Mass Concentration Units","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Density and the book's mass-concentration examples both have mass divided by volume, though the labels reflect different applications. Pryor converts lb/ft³ to kg/m³ and lb/gal to g/L. The mass factor belongs in the numerator; the volume ratio is inverted to cancel the original denominator. A numerically correct mass conversion alone therefore cannot give the right density. The unit structure also distinguishes these measures from mass alone. See [[Volume Unit Scaling]] and [[Conversion-Factor Chains]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions","Volume Unit Scaling","Conversion-Factor Chains","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Density and Mass Concentration Units.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Density and Mass Concentration Units.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"density and mass concentration units density and mass concentration units","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Density and Mass Concentration Units.md","fileName":"Density and Mass Concentration Units.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Density and Mass Concentration Units","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions","Volume Unit Scaling","Conversion-Factor Chains","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}